# Domain language

When naming a concept in issues, tests, UI copy, ADRs, or code comments, use `CONTEXT.md` terms. Do not drift to the avoided synonyms.

## Required terms

| Use | Avoid |
| --- | --- |
| Outcome Market | Contract, Strike Market, bare Market |
| Venue Market | Outcome Market (for the book), bare Market |
| Market Phase | Raw state, Active (in UI copy) |
| Trading Day | Calendar day, expiry date |
| Strike | Target price, exercise price |
| Yes Token / No Token | Call/put token, bullish/bearish coin |
| Pair | Bundle |
| Directional Intent | Raw order-book operation |
| Market Action | Market order, partial-fill order |
| Executable Depth | Liquidity, book size |
| Worst Execution Price | Slippage default, estimated price |
| Position State | Token balance, wallet balance (when meaning exposure) |
| Exposure Interval | Net balance, current exposure |
| Flat / Yes-sided / No-sided / Mixed / Unknown Position | Empty wallet, long/short, hedged, invalid balance |
| Recovery-only Mode | Offline mode, read-only mode |
| Directional Guardrail | Position invariant, Position Constraint |
| Mark Price | Current price, last price |
| Implied Probability | Bare “probability” or “prediction” |
| Live Underlying Price | Official Close, settlement price, current price |
| Collateral Liability / Surplus | Pairs minted, protocol fee |
| Rent Refund Address | Current authority, collateral/fee recipient |
| Redemption / Pair Redemption / Outcome Redemption | Burn, withdrawal, claim (as the family name) |
| Direct Holder Burn | Redemption, withdrawal |
| Official Close | Daily bar close, last price, after-hours/adjusted close |
| Close Method | Price source, aggregate type |
| Settlement Record | Price update, latest quote |
| Settlement Quality Predicate | Confidence interval, latest value |
| Settlement | Expiry, market close |
| Settlement Disputed | Void, draw, canceled market |
| Manual Settlement Override | Admin outcome, forced winner |
| Emergency Expiry | Pause, abandonment |
| Corporate Action Blackout | Split adjustment, adjusted close |
| History Completeness | Recent activity, best-effort history |
| Platform-execution P&L | Tax basis, total wallet P&L |
| Internal Unwind | Trade, realized sale |

## Guardrail semantics (ADR-0009, ADR-0019)

Evaluate Exposure Interval across wallet holdings, venue balances, and resting **and locally pending** orders. Mixed and Unknown fail closed for new Directional Intents. Missing indexed state enters Recovery-only Mode. Cancellation, fund settlement, Pair Redemption, and exit recovery remain available.

## Redemption semantics (ADR-0003)

Destruction through Meridian is a family: Pair Redemption (before **and** after Settlement in V1), market-assisted Pair Redemption for Sell No (live session only), and Outcome Redemption. Direct Holder Burn is unsupported classic SPL forfeiture, not Redemption.

## Settlement semantics (ADR-0012, 0021, 0023, 0026)

Every Outcome Market for a ticker and Trading Day consumes one Settlement Record. Official Close is the primary listing market’s unadjusted close (Nasdaq NOCP for V1). Missing Official Close is Settlement Disputed, not a substituted last trade.
